Microsoft Entra ID authentication protocols use nonce-based challenge-response mechanisms that prevent replay attacks. OAuth 2.0 tokens include timestamps, audience restrictions, and single-use authorization codes. FIDO2 security keys and Windows Hello for Business use cryptographic challenge-response that is inherently replay-resistant.
